# G8 (make check-setest): the testcases of upstream's setest suite that this
# fork answers differently from upstream's library. Both are built as
# SETEST_CFLAGS says, so the fixes behind SWE_UPSTREAM_COMPAT (those through
# ts.19) answer as upstream and are not here. One line per testcase: its id
# and the notes/UPSTREAM-BUGS.md entries that move it. setestcases.py
# compares; `make setest-record` rewrites the list, keeping each line's
# entries and marking a new testcase '?' for the change that moved it to
# explain.
#
# ts.20, 814 testcases:
#   6.8.361-720    bug 24: swe_houses_ex2() with SEFLG_RADIANS answers its
#                  speeds in radians (upstream: degrees); bug 44 moves their
#                  last digits
#   10.7, 10.8     bug 40: swe_helio_cross() and swe_helio_cross_ut(), and
#   1.1 (8)        heliocentric positions: the light time from the Sun
#   1.3, 8, 9      bug 39: topocentric positions, the eclipses and
#                  occultations at a place, and the heliacal functions, with
#                  the observer on the true pole; bug 44 moves 53 of the 61
#   5.4.1          bug 44: the equation of time
#
